EntityDescription,"A blink dog pup, already able to flicker away from danger before it lands a bite.",
EntityDescription,A bulbous fungus that bursts into a hissing cloud of acid when disturbed.,
EntityDescription,A career officer with a ruined face and a habit of winning. He has never once fought alone.,
EntityDescription,"A cave bear whose pelt has gone grey as cinders, hardened by years sheltered in a live volcano's roots.",
EntityDescription,"A cave spider drained of all colour by lightless generations, hunting by web-thrum alone.",
EntityDescription,"A cobra pale as hoarfrost, coiled in the ice caves where warm-blooded prey seeks shelter.",
EntityDescription,"A coyote with a static-charged coat, drawn down from the high plains after a lightning storm.",
EntityDescription,"A dead tree animated by rot and old malice, its bark split open where a jaw shouldn't be.",
EntityDescription,A dwarf of a mountain clan so far north the forge-fires burn blue; one of its twin mattocks bites like the wind off the peak.,
EntityDescription,A fey hound that flickers between here and elsewhere; it fights alongside anyone it trusts.,
EntityDescription,"A giant bat with clouded, sightless eyes, navigating wholly by the shriek of its own echo.",
EntityDescription,"A giant beetle with a carapace of blue-white chitin, breath steaming with cold in the deep dark.",
EntityDescription,"A giant caked grey with volcanic ash, walking down from a smoking peak with a club still smoking at the tip.",
EntityDescription,"A giant in red who arrives once a year with a sack, and whose generosity is best not put to the test.",
EntityDescription,"A giant of the high glaciers, sheathed in rime; its breath alone can flash-freeze a puddle solid.",
EntityDescription,"A gila monster whose beaded hide glows dull orange along the seams, as if lit from beneath.",
EntityDescription,"A gnome who never left the deep tunnels, pale and stooped, at ease chewing through rock with a pickaxe.",
EntityDescription,"A golem cast from bronze rather than raw iron; where its cousin only staggers under a lightning strike, this one drinks the current and spits it back.",
EntityDescription,"A grey hatchling, already contemptuous of magic and of you.",
EntityDescription,"A halfling from before halflings had villages, clubbing at the world with whatever came to hand.",
EntityDescription,"A hare with a single straight horn, and no sense whatever of how small it is.",
EntityDescription,"A hatchling out of the fey courts: bright-eyed, quick, and already lying to you.",
EntityDescription,A hatchling that has already learned one word it should not know.,
EntityDescription,"A hatchling that keeps half-vanishing while you look at it, and has not yet worked out how to stop.",
EntityDescription,"A hound of the Astral plane, half-seen even when it stands still; it does not breathe or bleed.",
EntityDescription,"A hovering bead of acid, small enough to ignore and stupid enough to close the distance anyway.",
EntityDescription,A hovering note that will not stop rising.,
EntityDescription,"A humanoid automaton, articulated at every joint, still carrying out whatever it was last told to do.",
EntityDescription,"A jackal wasted by sickness, its ribs showing through a mangy hide; its bite festers.",
EntityDescription,A jelly black as a starless sky; things it touches for too long forget how alive they were.,
EntityDescription,A jelly that glows faintly like a coal; fire only makes it swell larger and angrier.,
EntityDescription,A jelly that reeks of rot; it dissolves flesh and gear alike to feed itself.,
EntityDescription,"A jelly the colour of a bruise, faintly crackling; touching it feels like brushing a doorknob after crossing a carpet in winter.",
EntityDescription,"A jelly the colour of glacier ice, cold to the touch and colder still if it touches back.",
EntityDescription,"A junior officer with a commission bought or earned, leading from the front because that is where he is watched.",
EntityDescription,"A knot of turning air about the size of a head. It has no face, and it follows you regardless.",
EntityDescription,"A kobold camouflaged in mottled green, more comfortable in the canopy than underground; it spits venom from a hollow reed.",
EntityDescription,A lizardman who took up a foreign discipline and mastered it. His two blades move faster than his bulk suggests they can.,
EntityDescription,"A long worm that burrows through permafrost, its segmented hide crusted with rime.",
EntityDescription,"A lynx with a rime-white winter coat, breath fogging even in a warm room.",
EntityDescription,A medium-sized creature prone to great ambition. Short-lived but ubiquitous; they are not to be underestimated.,
EntityDescription,"A panther whose black coat smoulders at the edges, leaving smoking pawprints on stone.",
EntityDescription,"A plump waterfowl, unbothered by dungeons so long as there is a puddle nearby.",
EntityDescription,"A pudding of black, viscid tar that oozes and smoulders at once; anything it swallows comes out cindered.",
EntityDescription,"A raven with feathers like beaten iron, riding the thunderheads and stooping with a crack of static.",
EntityDescription,"A rodent the size of a dog, cheek pouches bulging with whatever it last found on the floor.",
EntityDescription,"A sewer rat gone pure white and pink-eyed, blind from generations in unlit tunnels.",
EntityDescription,"A shade gone pale and crystalline, trailing frost wherever it drifts; the cold pours off it before it ever draws near.",
EntityDescription,A shambling corpse wrapped in weeping buboes; the sickness that killed it did not stop working when it died.,
EntityDescription,"A shark bred to lightless ocean trenches, its eyes filmed over and useless.",
EntityDescription,"A skeleton picked clean by something worse than time; its bones are black at the joints, and its touch draws the warmth out of the living.",
EntityDescription,A small heap of coins that isn't quite finished counting itself.,
EntityDescription,"A soldier of the host: armed, armoured, and entirely without doubt.",
EntityDescription,A sphere with a short temper and a shorter future.,
EntityDescription,"A spitting beetle whose glands have gone volcanic, hawking gobbets of burning pitch.",
EntityDescription,"A standing wave of brackish swamp water, thick with algae and old poison; nothing in it is fresh, and nothing about touching it is safe.",
EntityDescription,"A standing wave, loud enough to be solid. You feel it in your teeth before you see it.",
EntityDescription,"A troll that wandered too near a volcano and came out the other side wrong: its hide is cracked magma-rock, glowing at every seam.",
EntityDescription,"A turning column of wind: enormous, empty, and impossible to hit anywhere that counts.",
EntityDescription,A unicorn whose hide is scored with runes that no hand cut. Magic slides off it and comes back sharpened.,
EntityDescription,"A walking pool of acid, held in the shape of a body by something with an appetite.",
EntityDescription,"A warrior in the service of a house, thoroughly competent with everything he has ever been handed.",
EntityDescription,"A water moccasin gone jet black, all but invisible against a night-flooded cave pool.",
EntityDescription,"A weathered chest, until its lid splits open into a maw ringed with teeth.",
EntityDescription,"A winged steed with a human face, which crosses in a single stride what a horse crosses in a day.",
EntityDescription,"A young astral dog, still learning to keep all four paws on the material plane at once.",
EntityDescription,"A young mimic, its shapeshifting still crude — usually just a box that bites back.",
EntityDescription,"Amorphous beings who have no typical shape but often take on a translucent humanoid form. While unmistakable for anything other than a plasma-like ooze, this form enables the use of clothing and tools.",
EntityDescription,"An ancient race of towering recluses. Their terrifying size gives them immense strength, supplemented by a voracious diet of meats and minerals.",
EntityDescription,"An ape with a crackling, wire-taut hide, native to the thunderheads above the high peaks.",
EntityDescription,"An elf of the sunlit dunes, skin bronzed and eyes narrowed; its arrows are fletched with fire-hardened reed and fly burning.",
EntityDescription,"An ogre gone half-feral in the fens, its skin sallow and slick; its claws carry a rot no wound-dressing can clean.",
EntityDescription,An orc mummy exhumed from a barrow sealed under a cinder-field; its wrappings are charred and its grip sears whatever it holds.,
EntityDescription,"An orc that has made its home in the marshlands, its blade notched and slicked with venom drawn from swamp adders.",
EntityDescription,An orc who worked out that pockets are a good deal easier to open than skulls.,
EntityDescription,"Astral beings who are a vessel for the indomitable spirit of a vanquished adventurer. Having no motivations of their own, they are glad to permit the possession; for the deceased adventurer, it is a second chance at revenge or redemption. Born from astral matter, they are slightly built, translucent and can move freely through physical obstacles.",
EntityDescription,"Bare hands, bare feet, and a discipline that took thirty years in the dark to learn.",
EntityDescription,Beaten out of scrap tin by an apprentice who wanted to prove a point. It rattles as it walks.,
EntityDescription,"Beautiful, otherworldly beings characterised by their signature halo and feathered wings. Strongly attuned to the struggle between good and evil, they sense the divinity within anything they hold.",
EntityDescription,Beware this clockwork machine of war.,
EntityDescription,Bipedal mechanical automatons with nearly unbounded artificial intelligence. Powered by a molten core engine that requires a constant supply of raw metals and is susceptible to water damage.,
EntityDescription,"Cast in silver at ruinous expense, and worth it: nothing rots it, nothing charms it, and it never tires.",
EntityDescription,"Centuries of study, and a library underneath it that no scholar will ever be allowed to see.",
EntityDescription,"Devout, unarmed by preference, and armed by necessity rather more often than her order cares to admit.",
EntityDescription,"Digs up other people's tombs for a living, and has learned which ones to leave alone.",
EntityDescription,"Drow magic is taught underground, quietly, and it is used the same way.",
EntityDescription,"Enormous, unarmoured, and entirely uninterested in the finer points of anything.",
EntityDescription,"Everything has a price, and he will find yours before you have finished speaking.",
EntityDescription,"Everything that is left when a fire has finished, and still hot enough for it to matter.",
EntityDescription,"Fey creatures linked by powerful nature spirits to fuel their antics. They are stocky with furry lower bodies, cloven hooves of a goat and curled horns of a ram. Ribald and clever, they cheerfully lead hedonistic escapades of drinking, dancing and fighting.",
EntityDescription,"Fights without armour, without caution, and without any evident expectation of tomorrow.",
EntityDescription,"Follows for miles without making a sound, and then picks the moment.",
EntityDescription,"He carries a mace because canon law denied him the edge, and he has never once felt the restriction.",
EntityDescription,He does not fight. He arranges matters so that the fighting has already been decided.,
EntityDescription,He gave up on cures some years ago. The other trade paid better and asked far fewer questions.,
EntityDescription,"He has fought campaigns you have only heard rumours of, and he expects the men behind him to keep up.",
EntityDescription,"He offers you exactly what you wanted, and the price is not mentioned until afterwards.",
EntityDescription,"He spent a lifetime learning to call the dead, and now they come whether he calls them or not.",
EntityDescription,"He wants your purse rather than your life, and will take the second only if you insist on it.",
EntityDescription,"Imposing and heavily built, they resemble humanoid dragons with a snout, scaly hide and functional wings.",
EntityDescription,"It drifts in and out of the here and now, and its breath arrives from somewhere that is not quite the room.",
EntityDescription,It has been playing the same joke for eight hundred years and has not yet reached the end of it.,
EntityDescription,It has spent so long between the planes that it is only visiting this one. Distance means nothing to it.,
EntityDescription,"It hoards grimoires the way other dragons hoard gold, and it has read them.",
EntityDescription,"It is holding itself together, and it is not going to manage that for very much longer.",
EntityDescription,It keeps the courtesies of the fey courts exactly as far as they amuse it.,
EntityDescription,"It sings the same three phrases in a voice that used to belong to somebody, and it will not be interrupted.",
EntityDescription,"It waits among the headstones shaped like one more grave marker, patient as the dead around it.",
EntityDescription,"It was built to stand in one place and stop things, and it is still doing exactly that long after the builders left.",
EntityDescription,Its scales drink spells the way sand drinks water. Wizards have learned to leave grey dragons alone.,
EntityDescription,"Large, omnivorous reptilians whose bestial ancestors dominated the world long before the birth of civilisation. They are fearsome predators, capable of leaping impressive distances and warding off many attacks with their thick scaly hides.",
EntityDescription,"Mixes what should not be mixed and takes careful notes, on the occasions when he survives to write them.",
EntityDescription,Monstrous creatures with the head and tail of a bull and the body of a man.,
EntityDescription,"More prankster than predator, which is not the same as harmless.",
EntityDescription,"Not the plump children of paintings: four faces, a great many wings, and a mandate to guard.",
EntityDescription,"Nothing cast at a grey dragon has ever much troubled it, and it knows this better than you do.",
EntityDescription,"Old blood, old grudges, and a sword that has been in the family longer than the family has held the land.",
EntityDescription,"Old enough that magic simply stops happening near it. Whatever it was once, it is now a hole in the weave.",
EntityDescription,"Old enough to have forgotten more magic than most schools teach, and to still remember the dangerous parts.",
EntityDescription,"Old, bent, and owed favours by things that ought not to be in a position to owe favours.",
EntityDescription,"Past apprentice, short of master, and painfully aware of the distance between the two.",
EntityDescription,"Perverse creatures of many aberrations but always with crimson skin and horns. Their mere presence compels others to act out their darkest, most violent desires.",
EntityDescription,"Rank-and-file infantry, drilled to hold a line with a spear and a shield, and to break it for nobody.",
EntityDescription,"Ravenous, predatory species of monstrous humanoid with a severe hunch that causes the backs of their hands to drag on the ground. Despite the awkward physical appearance, they are powerfully built and are infamous for their ability to rapidly recover from any wound to their rubbery hide.",
EntityDescription,Raw current given legs. The air around it tastes of a storm that has not arrived yet.,
EntityDescription,Scales like the silver void between the planes. It steps out of the world when it is losing.,
EntityDescription,"Sees perfectly in the dark, moves perfectly in it, and is already behind you.",
EntityDescription,"Shape-shifting deviants, who thrive on their deceptive talents.",
EntityDescription,"She is friendly, and she is interested in you, and neither of those things is true.",
EntityDescription,She rules a court of nymphs and has never yet had to raise a hand to keep it.,
EntityDescription,"She speaks for the spider goddess, and the enclave does whatever she says the goddess wants.",
EntityDescription,She tracks for a week and shoots once.,
EntityDescription,"She was beautiful once, in the way a knife is beautiful, and the resemblance has not altogether faded.",
EntityDescription,Small folk who prefer simple lives. They are notably gregarious and their build lends them well to less-than-noble endeavours.,
EntityDescription,"Small, old, and patient. He has outlived every hunter who assumed that size was the point.",
EntityDescription,"Small, wary, and quicker with a thrown rock than anyone her size has any right to be.",
EntityDescription,"Somebody built a machine, somebody else turned it, and a third party handed it a pistol. All three came to regret their part.",
EntityDescription,"Something enormous came up out of the deep water, and the deep water was glad to be rid of it.",
EntityDescription,"Spiritual beings fond of nature and magic. They are physically similar to humans, but often smaller and nimbler.",
EntityDescription,"Stands at the door of the tomb with a blade in either hand, and has been standing there a very long time.",
EntityDescription,"Steeped in high magic, and quite capable of being something else by the time you swing.",
EntityDescription,"Stout, short and hardy folk. They are known for their stubbornness, metalworking and love of alcohol.",
EntityDescription,"Subterranean peoples of diminutive stature, fond of tinkering and magic. Evolved for subsistence living, their metabolism is suited for long adventures where food is scarce.",
EntityDescription,"The burning ones. They stand nearest the throne, and everything near them catches.",
EntityDescription,"The first rank of the air school, who has learned to feel the wind before it moves.",
EntityDescription,"The highest rank of the air school. Where she is standing, the weather is a matter of her preference.",
EntityDescription,"The least of the host, made of fire and formed for one errand at a time.",
EntityDescription,"The lesser of the two ferrozygotic puddings, the brown pudding is said to taste more akin to rotted milk than a chocolate dessert. The pudding itself feeds upon fabrics and hides of all kind but its most known ability is its unique reproductive method. When brought into contact with iron the miracle of rotten slime binary fission takes place, creating two voracious offspring. Owing to the ubiquity of iron in the arms wielded by adventurers, this creature's population has only been growing with time.","Меньшая из двух феррумзиготных масс - кафяв масса, которая по вкусу сродни прокисшему молоку, чем шоколадному десерту. Питается всеми видами тканей и шкур. Уникальная способность бурой массы - репродуктивный метод. Когато масса вступает в контакт с железом, происходит её деление на два. Ввиду повсеместного использования железного оружия авантюристами, популяция этого существа только выросла."
EntityDescription,"The one who taught the soldiers their drill, and who fights rather better than any of them.",
EntityDescription,"The second rank, who no longer asks the wind for anything but simply takes it.",
EntityDescription,"The wheels within wheels, rimmed with eyes, turning without ever facing away.",
EntityDescription,"The white tiger of the west, in whose season metal is forged and old things are cut away.",
EntityDescription,"The young of the pheral: all claws, and no patience whatever.",
EntityDescription,"Thirty years of the same forms, every morning without exception, and now he needs no weapon at all.",
EntityDescription,"This mummy confection was created by steeping a human cadaver in honey. Somehow reanimated by an obscure cult of monks, it is both deadly and delicious.",
EntityDescription,This strange living bubble of corrosive fluids doesn't appear to have any offensive capabilities.,"Това ет странный живой пузырь, наполненный едкой жидкостью, не проявляет агрессии."
EntityDescription,"Tiny winged spirits, inherently magical and extraordinarily beautiful. When threatened, they can escape through distortions in spatial reality.",
EntityDescription,"Tortoise-like nomadic survivalists who leave their birthplace, from the moment they can walk, to travel the world with the comfort and protection of home on their backs.",
EntityDescription,"Ugly, brutish creatures with cannibalistic tendencies; this warlike race is known for their impressive strength and intellectual incapabilities.",
EntityDescription,"Unfairly characterised as cowardly and weak, these diminutive reptilian creatures overcome their physical limitations by employing vicious and cunning strategies.",
EntityDescription,Walks the roads between towns carrying everything he owns and a very good stick.,
EntityDescription,"Wrapped, crowned, and extremely displeased to have been woken.",
EntityDescription,"You do not meet an assassin. You meet somebody else, once, and after that you meet nobody at all.",
